In collaboration with Propelland and Cuerva Energy, Granada. The main objective of the project is to teach people how smart grids work. We headed to the south of Spain to interview end-users in their environment.

With the data gathered from the interviews, we designed a monolith that could be easily placed in the main square of the cities, which interactively explains to users what smart grids are and how energy reaches their homes. They can play a game using the totem which tests their knowledge and ranks them among players of the village.\
\
[Case Study](https://propelland.com/works/cuerva-living-labs/)
